  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electricity Transmission Sector Reforms Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed program aims to strengthen the structure of the transmission subsector and the institutional environment of Georgia?s electricity transmission company, the Joint-Stock Company Georgian State Electrosystem (GSE), and thereby enhance the transmission subsector?s efficiency and improve its financial aspects. These reforms are critical to strengthen GSE?s corporate governance, financial management, transparency, and debt sustainability. The program will be supported by the Asian Development Bank (ADB) through a single tranche stand-alone PBL, with a post-program engagement framework (PPEF).  The proposed program is in line with the Asian Development Bank (ADB) country partnership strategy for Georgia, 2014-2018.</narrative>
  </description>
